<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia July 1-25 palm oil exports 580,916t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia July 1-25 palm oil exports 580,916t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd on Friday it said it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for July 1-25 at 580,916 tonnes against 510,578 tonnes for June 1-25.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 166,635 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 239,605 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 76,245 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products totalled 98,431 tonnes.  </p>
<p>India was the top buyer during the period, taking 85,906 tonnes, followed by China which bought 77,850 tonnes, Egypt (67,645 tonnes) and Pakistan (56,450 tonnes).</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 70,750 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-275-6834)</p>
</text>
